  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "form all perfect tenses with haber + past participle",
        "use the past perfect for something that happened before another past event",
        "use the future perfect and conditional perfect for completion, probability and would-have",
        "use the present perfect subjunctive (espero que hayas llegado)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. One pattern, five tenses"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Every perfect tense is a form of <b>haber</b> + the <b>past participle</b> (A2 PDF 5). Only the tense of haber changes. The participle never changes: <i>he hecho, habíamos hecho, habrán hecho</i>."
    },
