    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Sequence of events",
      "text": "Use the preterite for the later event and the past perfect for the earlier one: <b>Cuando llegamos</b> (preterite), <b>ya habían empezado</b> (past perfect). If the order is clear from the words (<i>antes, después</i>), Spanish often uses just the preterite."
    },
